---
// salt-loop — the central idea of the γ-MSH page. A high-sodium diet raises
// pituitary POMC processing to γ-MSH and plasma γ-MSH; γ-MSH acting through
// MC3R promotes sodium excretion, closing a negative-feedback loop that keeps
// blood pressure steady on a salty diet. Break the loop — no MC3R, no PC2 to
// make γ-MSH, or an MC3R blocker — and the same diet produces salt-sensitive
// hypertension (Ni et al. 2003). A side note: γ-MSH injected into the brain
// raises blood pressure through a different, amiloride-sensitive route, not
// MC3R (Ni et al. 2006). Schematic; SVG-only, wrap in <Figure>.
---

<svg
  class="salt-fig"
  viewBox="0 0 640 300"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="salt-t salt-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="salt-t">The salt loop: how γ-MSH and MC3R defend blood pressure on a high-sodium diet</title>
  <desc id="salt-d"
    >A four-step loop. A high-sodium diet raises pituitary γ-MSH production;
    γ-MSH rises in the blood; it acts through MC3R, by a route that appears to
    run through the nervous system rather than the kidney itself; sodium
    excretion rises, and blood pressure stays normal. Beneath the loop, three
    ways of breaking it — deleting MC3R, deleting the enzyme PC2 that makes
    γ-MSH, or blocking MC3R with an antagonist — all produce salt-sensitive
    hypertension in rodents. A side panel notes that γ-MSH injected into the
    brain raises blood pressure through an amiloride-sensitive sodium channel,
    independent of MC3R.</desc
  >

  <!-- loop nodes -->
  <rect class="card" x="20" y="30" width="140" height="58" rx="12" />
  <text x="90" y="54" text-anchor="middle" class="head">High-sodium diet</text>
  <text x="90" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">the challenge</text>

  <rect class="card hot" x="190" y="30" width="140" height="58" rx="12" />
  <text x="260" y="54" text-anchor="middle" class="head hot-t">Pituitary γ-MSH ↑</text>
  <text x="260" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">POMC → PC2 → γ-MSH</text>

  <rect class="card hot" x="360" y="30" width="140" height="58" rx="12" />
  <text x="430" y="54" text-anchor="middle" class="head hot-t">MC3R</text>
  <text x="430" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">likely via neural routes</text>

  <rect class="card" x="530" y="30" width="90" height="58" rx="12" />
  <text x="575" y="54" text-anchor="middle" class="head">Na⁺ out</text>
  <text x="575" y="72" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">natriuresis</text>

  <!-- forward arrows -->
  <path class="branch hot" d="M160 59 L190 59" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="182,54 190,59 182,64" />
  <path class="branch hot" d="M330 59 L360 59" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="352,54 360,59 352,64" />
  <path class="branch hot" d="M500 59 L530 59" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="522,54 530,59 522,64" />

  <!-- return arrow: Na out → blood pressure steady → back to the start -->
  <path class="branch" d="M575 88 L575 118 L90 118 L90 88" />
  <polygon class="arrow dimfill" points="85,96 95,96 90,88" />
  <text x="332" y="113" text-anchor="middle" class="tag">blood pressure stays normal — the loop closes</text>

  <!-- travelling dot -->
  <circle class="pulse" r="4">
    <animateMotion dur="4.2s" repeatCount="indefinite" keyPoints="0;1" keyTimes="0;1"
      path="M160 59 L530 59" />
  </circle>

  <!-- ===== broken loop ===== -->
  <text x="20" y="160" class="head">Break any link and the same diet raises blood pressure</text>

  <rect class="card dim" x="20" y="174" width="180" height="50" rx="10" />
  <text x="110" y="194" text-anchor="middle" class="line">no MC3R</text>
  <text x="110" y="211" text-anchor="middle" class="mini">Mc3r-knockout mouse</text>

  <rect class="card dim" x="214" y="174" width="180" height="50" rx="10" />
  <text x="304" y="194" text-anchor="middle" class="line">no γ-MSH</text>
  <text x="304" y="211" text-anchor="middle" class="mini">PC2-knockout mouse</text>

  <rect class="card dim" x="408" y="174" width="212" height="50" rx="10" />
  <text x="514" y="194" text-anchor="middle" class="line">MC3R blocked</text>
  <text x="514" y="211" text-anchor="middle" class="mini">antagonist-treated rat</text>

  <path class="branch" d="M320 224 L320 244" />
  <polygon class="arrow dimfill" points="315,236 325,236 320,244" />
  <rect class="card warn" x="200" y="244" width="240" height="30" rx="10" />
  <text x="320" y="264" text-anchor="middle" class="head">salt-sensitive hypertension</text>

  <!-- side note -->
  <text x="20" y="292" class="line">Separately: γ-MSH injected into the brain raises blood pressure — via an amiloride-sensitive channel, not MC3R.</text>
</svg>

